WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Maya Chen>Thanks for making time, Alex. Last time you mentioned the rollout was blocked on your security team.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Alex Park>Right. Honestly that's still the blocker. Our CISO won't sign off on anything that stores customer data outside the EU, and we've been burned by vendors before.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Maya Chen>That makes sense, and I'd rather solve it now than at procurement. Two things: we host EU customers in Frankfurt only, and we're SOC 2 Type II. I can send the report and our data processing agreement today, and offer a 30 minute call between your CISO and our security lead this week.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
<v Alex Park>That would help a lot. If the CISO is comfortable, budget is already approved for this quarter.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Maya Chen>Great. What's the approved range, so I scope the right package?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Alex Park>Around one eighty for the first year.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Maya Chen>Perfect. So next step: I send the SOC 2 report and DPA today, and we book the security call for Thursday. Does 2pm work?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Alex Park>Thursday 2pm works. Send the invite.
